[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Beryllium is a development build (Phase 1).

Sandbox status: none by default. Like www/chromium today, no Beryllium
process runs in Capsicum capability mode, and beryllium://gpu says
"Sandboxed: false". An experimental renderer lockdown, not yet a complete
sandbox, can be tried with:
    beryllium --enable-features=BerylliumCapsicumRenderer
Do not rely on this release to contain a compromised web page. The sandbox
status of each release is published at https://github.com/johnjanik/Beryllium.

- Manual pages: beryllium(1) for the command, its options, environment
  and files; beryllium-sandbox(7) for what is confined and how to check.
- Updates: install a newer Beryllium package (install.sh, or a new
  Poudriere build); there is no in-browser updater.
- Profile: ~/.config/beryllium (override with BERYLLIUM_CONFIG_HOME).
- Fonts: text is drawn with whatever installed font has its glyphs. The
  package brings Noto Sans (Latin, Greek, Cyrillic), Noto Sans CJK SC
  (Chinese, Japanese, Korean) and Noto Color Emoji. For other scripts
  install their fonts, for example noto-sans-arabic, noto-sans-hebrew,
  noto-sans-devanagari, noto-sans-thai, or all of them with noto-extra
  (250 MB). `fc-list :lang=xx` shows what covers a language.
- Policies: %%PREFIX%%/etc/beryllium/policies/managed/
- Wayland is recommended. Under X11, any program in the session can read
  input from and inject input into other windows.
- Online services (extension proxy, !bangs list, filter-list and component
  updates, dictionaries) are off, and no server is built in: Beryllium runs
  none of its own yet. To use them, turn them on and enter a server at
  beryllium://settings/privacy/services.
- Optional system hardening that blocks some cross-process observation:
    sysctl security.bsd.see_other_uids=0
    sysctl security.bsd.see_other_gids=0
    sysctl security.bsd.unprivileged_proc_debug=0   (also stops users
      debugging their own programs)
- kern.ipc.shm_allow_removed=1 is required (the launcher checks it).
EOM
}
]
